      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ok6gr75s",
      "title": "What I practiced ",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "6e9o44kr",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "6h636ocq",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "What I took from it"
              },
              {
                "id": "pa1a3fo6",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "Holding one accent colour. Keeping red for action only, across a whole page, was harder and more useful than adding more colour would have been.",
                  "Motion as layout. The diagonals and the running figures make the page feel like it is moving before anything animates.",
                  "Interaction with restraint. The category row hides its detail until hover, so the page stays calm until you ask it for more.",
                  "Copy is part of the design. The first pass reused one line everywhere, and rewriting each section to stand on its own taught me that filler text undoes good layout faster than a bad grid does."
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "insight"
    },
    {
      "id": "9bll4mx0",
      "title": "Honest note",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "hnzbr0a0",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "o5miwn1s",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "For the record"
              },
              {
                "id": "wj18m8xq",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "HOBZ UP is a concept I designed for myself, not a real store and not client work. Everything here, brand and all, is mine, made to practice a direction I do not get to use every day."
              },
              {
